2. Upstream-derived files — NOT covered by the MIT grant above
--------------------------------------------------------------
This project derives from NaClwww's "Mobile Network" DMS plugin:
    https://github.com/NaClwww/dms-modem-plugin
That upstream ships no LICENSE file, which by default means all rights are
reserved by its author. The following files contain substantial portions
derived from it, and are therefore excluded from the MIT grant in section 1:

    docs/NETWORKMANAGER_BACKEND.md    predominantly upstream text
    StartupCheck.qml                  predominantly upstream code
    ModemSettings.qml                 predominantly upstream code
    ModemWidget.qml                   predominantly upstream code
    plugin.json                      upstream structure with edits
    README.md                         upstream sections with edits
    assets/control-center.png         upstream asset, unchanged
    Store.qml                         upstream core with large additions

No licence is claimed over those files in this repository, and this file does
not relicense them. They remain under whatever terms their upstream author
has set (currently: no license at all).

Permission to keep redistributing them is being requested from the upstream
author via NaClwww/dms-modem-plugin#2 and by e-mail (both opened 2026-10-02).
Until that permission exists:

  * registry maintainers should treat those files as unlicensed, and may
    reject this entry or request its removal at any time;
  * the MIT statement above applies only to section 1 of this file.

If the upstream author grants a licence, this file will be updated to name
it, and the scope of the MIT grant will be restated accordingly.
